{
 "schema": "zrmd/music-studio@1",
 "date": "14 October 2026",
 "doc": "Interface of Scripts/MusicStudio.py (HDA law): the twelve procedural values (4 primary and 8 secondary, see params/v1-tiers.json) a person changes to make a variation of a music track, and how each one reaches the engine. mode 'render' = the engine re-renders the track from params.json (about half a minute, the reference stays unreachable); mode 'live' = also previewed instantly in the browser on the rendered stems, exact at the next render. apply.kind: tempo, transpose, stemGain, voiceMacro (every voice that has the macro), voiceMacroScale (multiplies the macro of tonal voices). FR : les huit valeurs procedurales d'une variation musicale et la facon dont chacune atteint le moteur. voiceMacroFor: adds (op add) or multiplies (op scale) a macro of NAMED voices from the voice's own calibrated value, so a calibrated voice keeps its character.",
